From c3826bc61b812b776b95ac64a320ed4dfeaba492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yury Klushin <digger@live.ru>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 09:48:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Make pdp11rt11rel's relocation constants p-sect-relative

A REL relocation entry's constant is relative to the p-sect the entry
names -- the RT-11 loader adds that p-sect's own base to it.  The
value being written came straight out of the `-r` output's own
layout (.text at 0, .data right after it, .bss after that), which is
the same thing only for .text, whose start is 0.  A reference into
.data was therefore relocated by .data's offset twice, and stayed
unnoticed until the first PPU program with a jump table there.

Take the target section's start back out.  Displaced (PC-relative)
entries keep the raw self-relative word, which does not depend on
where the module loads.
---
 ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11rel.em | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11rel.em b/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11rel.em
index 8a7e691e177..fcb67d8ac1c 100644
--- a/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11rel.em
+++ b/ld/emultempl/pdp11rt11rel.em
@@ -642,6 +642,21 @@ rel_write_section (FILE *f, bfd *ibfd, struct rel_psect_info *psect,
 	  sym = *rel->sym_ptr_ptr;
 	  kind = rel_classify_symbol (sym, psects);
 
+	  /* The raw word holds the target's address in this \`-r\` output's
+	     own layout (.text at 0, .data right after it, .bss after
+	     that), but a REL constant is relative to the *p-sect* the
+	     entry names -- the loader adds that p-sect's own base to it.
+	     Take the target section's start back out, or a reference
+	     into .data ends up relocated by .data's offset twice
+	     (harmless for .text, whose start is 0 -- which is how this
+	     went unnoticed until the first PPU program with a .data
+	     jump table).  Displaced (PC-relative) entries keep the raw
+	     self-relative word: nothing in it depends on where the
+	     module loads.  */
+	  if (!pcrel && kind != PSECT_NONE && kind != PSECT_ABS)
+	    constant = (constant - (unsigned int) psects[(int) kind].sec->vma)
+		       & 0xffff;
+
 	  if (kind == PSECT_NONE)
 	    {
 	      /* A real external symbol.  */
